cat > DEVELOPMENT.md <<'EOF'
# Building and testing

This checkout contains an independent C++17 implementation of the documented
command-line application. It uses the general-purpose libgit2 library for Git
storage and transport, and POSIX interfaces for terminal input and subprocesses.

Build the executable in the repository root:

```sh
./compile.sh
./executable --help
```

The build requires a C++17 compiler and the libgit2 development package. The
build script checks for these and installs them on Debian-compatible systems
when necessary. No application-specific packages or source downloads are used.

Run the regression suite with Python 3 and Git available:

```sh
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

The tests isolate configuration and repositories in temporary directories. They
cover setup, configuration errors, argument parsing, literal editor/pager
invocations, branch switching, commits, and pushes to a local bare repository.

## Source layout

- `src/main.cpp`: command-line processing, logging, terminal input, subprocesses
- `src/config.cpp`: configuration paths, JSON reading/writing, setup and clearing
- `src/git.cpp`: viewing, editing, staging, committing and pushing ideas
- `tests/test_behavior.py`: command-line regression tests

All generated executables and intermediate build files are ignored by Git.
